I took this Cisco Linksys E900 for a spin this week and was impressed.  I just converted over to two Medialink Wireless N routers earlier this year and have they have not lived up to the (some potential fake) reviews on Amazon.  The main gripe with my Medialinks is they have weak wireless signals around the house (one for main floor, one for basement).  Here's my story:
  -I plugged this basic Linksys in directly next to my Medialink;
  -Setup was very easy on this Linksys, I just put the CD in my computer and clicked through and then done and up and running (it really did just take minutes & was easier than the Medialink setup);
  -Sitting in the same cabinet as my Medialink - the Linksys has better signal around my main floor.  I connected to my Kindle Fire no problem - good speeds (better than my other wireless router).

And finally what I also like is this router does not have lights in the front.  The Medialink has all kinds of unnecessary crazy blue flashing lights in the front that are distracting if placed in a bedroom or a tv room (tip- put tape over the lights).  The Linksys has well thoughout light in the rear and I noticed in the software advanced setup there is even option to turn the light off.

So in conclusion, for $40 a great 5-star value based upon my initial experience, if anything changes I will add update to my review. I am actually tempted now to move to one of the higher end Linksys models now for even better signal.

